{
  "requirement": "`languages::PlainText` implements `OutlineLang` under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.outlines.language_provider`. Its default value is\ncheaply cloneable and claims no extensions. The filename-based constructors\nselect it when no supplied language claims the extension, including filenames\nwithout an extension, under {cite}`requirements.sdk.outlines.defaults`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The structural check finds no gap. The requirement's behavioral outcomes (the plain-text outline shape and the fallback result) were not independently assessed.\n\n- **`OutlineLang` implementation.** `crates/trust-but-verify/src/outline/languages/mod.rs` invokes `language!(PlainText, super::plain::PROFILE, \"plain-text-structural-v1\")`, and that invocation carries the `{impl}` reference. The `macro[language]` expands to `impl super::OutlineLang for PlainText`. It supplies all four required methods: `name`, `extensions`, `outline` (via `parse_with`) and `fingerprint_scheme`, plus `search_structure`. The `Clone + Send + Sync` bounds hold because the type is a unit struct.\n- **Default value, cheap clone, no extensions.**\n  - The macro declares `#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, Default)] pub struct PlainText;`, so it has a default value and clones trivially, with no configuration to rebuild or copy.\n  - `extensions()` returns `$profile.extensions`. In `crates/trust-but-verify/src/outline/plain.rs#static[PROFILE]` that is `&[]`, so no extensions are claimed.\n- **Filename-based fallback.**\n  - `crates/trust-but-verify/src/outline/contents.rs#impl[OutlineContent]/fn[from_source]` looks up `languages::registry().for_path(filename)`. When nothing matches, it calls `from_source_with(&languages::PlainText, ...)`.\n  - `Registry::for_path` in `language.rs` returns `None` when `path.extension()` is absent, and otherwise matches on the lowercased extension. Filenames without an extension therefore fall through to `PlainText`.\n  - `from_path` also reaches this fallback, though I did not read its body. `profile_for_path` in `profile.rs` has the same plain fallback.\n- **Delegated obligations.** The `defaults` and `language_provider` requirements are cited context only. The \"file root with one child per nonblank line\" outline shape belongs to `defaults` and the plain-text outline rules, so I did not assess it here.\n\nAll structural obligations are supported by the sources above, and there are no {fixme} acknowledgments to account for.",
